meta {
  name: Rerun Auto-Assignment
  type: http
  seq: 90
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lead-assignment/rerun?tenant_id={{tenantId}}&dry_run=true
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "org_ids": [],
    "campaign_type_ids": []
  }
}

docs {
  Super-admin console action: re-runs auto-assignment for leads that arrived
  UNASSIGNED (their pool had nobody eligible) once an admin has fixed the
  weights or the role's department.

  dry_run defaults to true. Flip to false to actually assign.

  Only fills gaps — never touches a lead that has an owner, any logged
  interaction, a terminated stage, or is superseded/inactive.

  Returns { dry_run, candidates, assigned, left_unassigned, remaining,
  next_cursor, by_branch[{ org_name, campaign_type_label, assigned,
  left_unassigned, reasons: { no_weighted_users, no_department_match,
  no_capable_users } }] }. At most 500 leads per call: pass next_cursor back as
  body.cursor to continue.

  Regression checks:
    * dry_run=true writes nothing (before/after SELECT on lms.marketing_leads)
    * a branch whose only Hiring-weighted user has a Sales role -> left
      unassigned, reasons.no_department_match
    * dry_run=false -> lead_assignment_log rows with action 'initial', the
      re-run note and "From the <type> pool."
    * an org_id from another tenant            -> 400
    * a bogus tenant_id                         -> 404
    * caller below super_admin                  -> 403 (gateway)
}
